00:41:38.420 --> 00:41:39.420
keeping it current.

00:41:39.420 --> 00:41:42.620
I think that you're doing a public service, and this is very important.

00:41:42.620 --> 00:41:46.460
Yeah, but you know what, we're not going to reach that many people.

00:41:46.460 --> 00:41:47.620
Let's cut to the chase here.

00:41:47.620 --> 00:41:48.900
We always hear that.

00:41:48.900 --> 00:41:52.160
You do good work, and yeah, and there's a public service.

00:41:52.160 --> 00:41:55.800
The fact of the matter is Daniel Ellsberg's revelations

00:41:55.800 --> 00:41:58.400
were not able to stop the Vietnam War.

00:41:58.400 --> 00:42:02.120
And you know, we're right now legitimately horrified,

00:42:02.120 --> 00:42:05.600
say, by what the Russians are doing in Ukraine

00:42:05.600 --> 00:42:07.600
and killing civilians.

00:42:07.600 --> 00:42:11.320
You wanna compare that to the carpet bombing of Vietnam.

00:42:11.320 --> 00:42:14.080
You wanna compare that to the bombing

00:42:14.080 --> 00:42:15.520
of Japan and Germany in the war.

00:42:15.520 --> 00:42:19.920
I mean, but at least that was a full scale war, you know.

00:42:19.920 --> 00:42:22.840
But what Ellsberg revealed in the Pentagon Papers,

00:42:22.840 --> 00:42:24.920
a war that never made any sense.

00:42:24.920 --> 00:42:27.240
And the conservative estimates,

00:42:27.240 --> 00:42:30.560
McNamara once said he would be considered a war criminal

00:42:30.560 --> 00:42:32.200
if the wrong side had won.

00:42:32.200 --> 00:42:33.880
And with three and a half million,

00:42:33.880 --> 00:42:36.760
he admitted to that died there, mostly civilians.

00:42:36.760 --> 00:42:40.520
Now to figure, people think we're throwing Cambodia,

00:42:40.520 --> 00:42:42.360
you know, and Laos and so forth,

00:42:42.360 --> 00:42:45.320
probably between five and six, seven million

00:42:45.320 --> 00:42:50.120
died in a war that no one could make sense of, you know, we tore apart the whole Mideast

00:42:50.120 --> 00:42:57.360
or some area you know more about than probably anybody I could talk to for no rhyme or reason

00:42:57.360 --> 00:43:03.880
that made sense. And there's no accountability. We have this illusion that we are accountable

00:43:03.880 --> 00:43:10.360
and we're not. This is Rome. This is Rome. And they can cover it with fancy language.

00:43:10.360 --> 00:43:15.400
They can cover it with manners, but it's Rome on a rampage, you know?

00:43:15.400 --> 00:43:17.840
And that's really what's happening.

00:43:17.840 --> 00:43:26.000
The incredible assertion of the American prerogative, American power, and anything America does

00:43:26.000 --> 00:43:28.480
somehow is morally justifiable.

00:43:28.480 --> 00:43:29.480
Disagree?

00:43:29.480 --> 00:43:31.960
I couldn't agree more.

00:43:31.960 --> 00:43:33.600
I think you're exactly right.

00:43:33.600 --> 00:43:34.840
All right.

00:43:34.840 --> 00:43:36.360
Let's wrap it up then.

00:43:36.360 --> 00:43:39.280
That's it for this edition of Sheer Intelligence.

00:43:39.280 --> 00:43:42.160
I want to thank John Kiriakou, a very brave,

00:43:42.160 --> 00:43:47.160
a broke human being, I mean financially, not spiritually.

00:43:48.720 --> 00:43:51.000
I want to thank the folks at KCRW,

00:43:51.000 --> 00:43:55.480
the FM station in Santa Monica, the NPR station

00:43:55.480 --> 00:43:58.120
for putting this on, Christopher Ho, and the others.

00:43:58.120 --> 00:44:00.720
Joshua Sheer, our executive producer,

00:44:00.720 --> 00:44:03.920
Natasha Kimi Zapata, who does the introduction,

00:44:03.920 --> 00:44:06.240
Lucy Berber, who does the transcription.

00:44:06.240 --> 00:44:13.460
and the JKW Foundation in the memory of a very strong, independent writer, journalist,

00:44:13.460 --> 00:44:16.260
Jean Stein for helping support these shows.

00:44:16.260 --> 00:44:19.740
See you next week with another edition of Sheer Intelligence.

